"""
Program : EIMISR01.py
Purpose : Monthly report on savings deposits' outstanding balance
          (Report ID: DMMISR01) and accounts breakdown by branch,
          for PBB (conventional) & PIBB (Islamic) combined.

Notes on conversion:
  - Report date comes from ctl_dwh_batch_dttm.sas7bdat, SOURCE_SYSTEM_CD = DP.
    There is no dependency on REPTDATE / input_date / output_date.
  - DYPOSXBR&REPTMON (.sas7bdat) is resolved as DYPOSXBR{REPTMON}.sas7bdat
    under INPUT_DIR. It is converted to a temporary Parquet file, read via
    DuckDB, and the temporary file is deleted afterwards (no cache is kept).
  - LIBNAME MIS "SAP.PBB.MIS.D&REPTYEAR" is not applicable: there is no
    separate MIS_DIR input in this environment.
  - //ISR01 DD ... DCB=(...,RECFM=FB,...) -> RECFM=FB (not FBA), meaning
    the original output carries NO ASA carriage-control characters.
    The report is plain semicolon-delimited, fixed-column text.
  - The output file is SFTP'd to the Data Report Repository (DRR), folder
    "WMTB-SA&S/DEP - SAS/RM RPT/SA/OS BALANCE", as in the //RUNSFTP step.
  - The SFTP target filename SA_BAL&ACC@&REPTMON&REPTYR..TXT uses the macro
    variable &ACC, which is never assigned in the source. SAS leaves an
    unresolved reference as literal text, so it is kept literally (ACC_TOKEN).
"""




